            {
              "text": "Law firms located in and serving **Springfield and Greater Springfield, QLD** (including Springfield Central, Brookwater, and Augustine Heights) that handle **will contests, Family Provision Applications (FPAs), and estate litigation** include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Brookwater Legal**\n* **Location:** Suite 9F, 118 Augusta Parkway, Augustine Heights QLD (adjacent to Springfield Central / Orion Shopping Centre).\n* **Practice Focus:** Brookwater Legal has a dedicated wills, estates, and succession practice. They regularly act for both claimants and executors in contested estate matters across Greater Springfield and the wider Ipswich region. \n* **Litigation Services:** \n  * Family Provision Applications (claims for adequate maintenance and support).\n  * Challenging will validity (undue influence, lack of testamentary capacity, informal wills).\n  * Advising executors defending an estate against claims.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **McNamara Law**\n* **Location:** GE Building, Level 1, 6 Yoga Way, Springfield Central QLD.\n* **Practice Focus:** McNamara Law is one of the most established regional practices in Ipswich and Western Corridor/Springfield. Their estate litigation department handles contested estates.\n* **Litigation Services:**\n  * Court representation for Family Provision Applications in both the District and Supreme Courts of Queensland.\n  * Proving wills in solemn form when a will’s validity is attacked.\n  * Pursuing or defending claims regarding attorney misconduct/misappropriation under an Enduring Power of Attorney.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **GLG Legal Springfield (formerly Springfield Legal Service)**\n* **Location:** Brookwater Office Park, Building 9, Level 1/22 Magnolia Drive, Brookwater QLD.\n* **Practice Focus:** Having served the Springfield, Brookwater, and Ipswich corridors for over two decades, the firm has an active wills and estates practice dealing directly with estate disputes.\n* **Litigation Services:**\n  * Advising spouses, biological/stepchildren, and dependents excluded from a will or left insufficient provision.\n  * Resolving disputed superannuation death benefits and non-estate asset conflicts.\n  * Estate mediation and defending executors from distribution liabilities.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Keane Legal**\n* **Location:** Brookwater Office Park, Brookwater QLD (also in Ipswich).\n* **Practice Focus:** Keane Legal provides succession and estate planning services for the Greater Springfield and Western Suburbs communities, with an emphasis on dispute negotiation and court representation.\n* **Litigation Services:**\n  * Bringing and defending Family Provision Claims under the *Succession Act 1981 (Qld)*.\n  * Challenging wills on grounds of testamentary incapacity, fraud, or suspicious circumstances.\n  * Advising beneficiaries on their statutory rights to inspect estate documentation and accounting.\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Stanford Legal**\n* **Location:** Springfield Central / Ipswich corridor.\n* **Practice Focus:** Stanford Legal assists clients across Springfield with personal dispute resolution and estate conflicts.\n* **Litigation Services:**\n  * Family provision claims and negotiating settlement terms via pre-litigation mediation.\n  * Managing estate challenges where blended family dynamics or estranged family members are involved.\n\n---\n\n### Key Queensland Time Limits to Keep in Mind\nIf you are planning to bring an FPA or contest a will under the ***Succession Act 1981* (Qld)**:\n1. **6-Month Notice:** Written notice of your intention to claim must be formally given to the estate's executor/personal representative within **6 months** of the date of death.\n2. **9-Month Court Filing:** The formal originating application must be filed in the Supreme Court or District Court of Queensland within **9 months** of the date of death.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
